# 7. Payments

## POST /payments

Authenticated.

Creates a simulated payment for a booking.

Allowed only for a booking owned by the caller, in status `PENDING` or
`CONFIRMED`, with no existing `PAID` payment (see BR-037). The backend sets the
amount, transaction reference and status; the client sends neither.

For the normal college-demo flow, simulated payments succeed by default. A
successful payment for a `PENDING` booking transitions that booking to
`CONFIRMED`. A failed payment must not confirm the booking. The `FAILED` status
is only produced through a controlled test path; clients cannot submit their
own payment status or force a payment outcome.

### Request

```json
{
  "bookingId": "BOOKING_ID",
  "method": "UPI"
}
```

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Payment processed successfully.",
  "data": {
    "id": "PAYMENT_ID",
    "bookingId": "BOOKING_ID",
    "amount": 9000,
    "method": "UPI",
    "status": "PAID",
    "transactionReference": "SIM-123456"
  }
}
```

