# 8. Returns

## POST /returns

ADMIN only.

The admin processes the physical return on behalf of the customer. This endpoint
creates the return record and performs the associated booking transition:
`PICKED_UP -> RETURNED` or `OVERDUE -> RETURNED`. It must reject bookings that
are not eligible for return and must prevent duplicate return records.

### Request

```json
{
  "bookingId": "BOOKING_ID",
  "actualReturnDate": "2026-10-22",
  "condition": "GOOD"
}
```

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Return processed successfully.",
  "data": {
    "id": "RETURN_ID",
    "bookingId": "BOOKING_ID",
    "expectedReturnDate": "2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z",
    "actualReturnDate": "2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z",
    "lateDays": 2,
    "fine": 200,
    "condition": "GOOD",
    "status": "LATE"
  }
}
```

